  "input_elements": [
    {
      "id": "i1",
      "content": "To begin with, for CAB, the first step is to assess the change request."
    },
    {
      "id": "i2",
      "content": "the next step is to check the affected systems for any impacts on the business unit."
    },
    {
      "id": "i3",
      "content": "the next task is to determine whether the change request should be approved or not."
    },
    {
      "id": "i4",
      "content": "If the change request should be approved in its current state, then it is approved."
    },
    {
      "id": "i5",
      "content": "if the change request should not be approved in its current state, further evaluation is needed to determine if the change will be acceptable with more information provided."
    },
    {
      "id": "i6",
      "content": "If the change request is ultimately approved, the change is implemented."
    },
    {
      "id": "i7",
      "content": "On the other hand, if the change is deemed unacceptable, it is rejected."
    },
    {
      "id": "i8",
      "content": "In this case, a request for more information is made to the Change Coordinator."
    },
    {
      "id": "i9",
      "content": "The request is then followed by an email enquiry to the Change Coordinator."
    },
    {
      "id": "i10",
      "content": "the approval register is updated within a timeframe of 3 business days."
    },
    {
      "id": "i11",
      "content": "The email enquiry is also forwarded to the Change Requester."
    },
    {
      "id": "i12",
      "content": "If there are no further inquiries or issues, the process concludes after 3 business days."
    },
    {
      "id": "i13",
      "content": "However, if there are inquiries from the CAB, a response is expected within 1-3 business days."
    },
    {
      "id": "i14",
      "content": "Once the response is received from the requester, it is forwarded to the CAB for further evaluation."
    },
    {
      "id": "i15",
      "content": "Based on the response, a final determination is made regarding the approval of the change request."
    }
  ]
}